      "geometry": "rect",
      "text": "Data note: NCEP/NCAR R1 near-surface sigma995 wind and sea-level pressure SLP; maps show 2023 AMJ/JJA minus the 1982/1997/2015 composite. CWP means central-western Pacific. CWP low-level wind differences are -2.301 m/s in AMJ and -2.576 m/s in JJA; SOI-like SLP-gradient differences are positive. How to read: NCEP is still a fallback, but it already provides a clear clue: AMJ/JJA central-western Pacific low-level wind is weaker than in historical strong events, and the SLP gradient is not established in a canonical El Niño way.",
